I. DEFINITIONS

  “License” means these terms.

  “Copyright Holder” means Morgan Le Thuaut.

  “Licensee” or “you” means the individual or legal entity exercising rights
  under this License.

  “Software” means the upwwwards library and any related packages, plugins,
  tools, documentation, or materials made available by the Copyright Holder
  under this License (including npm distributions and updates).

  “Permitted Use” means implementing and/or using the Software, as provided,
  in a website, web application, digital product, or similar end-user-facing
  experience that you (or your client) own or operate — including commercial
  projects — where the Software is a dependency or runtime of that experience.

  Permitted Use also includes developing, distributing, and operating software
  packages, libraries, frameworks, and developer tools that use the Software as
  a dependency, provided that such products are not Competitive Products.

  “Competitive Product” means a software product whose primary purpose
  is to provide substantially similar functionality to the Software itself,
  and which is marketed or distributed as a substitute for the Software.

  A product shall not be considered a Competitive Product solely because
  it uses the Software as a dependency, integrates its APIs, or provides
  additional functionality built on top of the Software.


