  this License remains in effect and is not terminated under Section VI.

  You may modify the Software solely for your own internal use or for use in
  a Permitted Use, provided that such modifications are not distributed as a
  standalone library or as part of a Competitive Product. For clarity, this
  permission includes maintaining private forks or modified copies of the
  Software solely for internal use or for a Permitted Use.

  You may distribute the Software as a dependency of your own software package
  (for example, declaring it in package.json so that npm, pnpm, or yarn installs
  it for consumers of your package), provided that:

  (a) the Software is not redistributed as a standalone product;

  (b) the Software is not modified for that redistribution (consumers must
      receive the Software as published by the Copyright Holder, typically via
      the official package registry entry);

  (c) the distribution is solely intended to enable a Permitted Use; and

  (d) the distribution does not grant recipients any rights beyond those
      expressly granted under this License (recipients are licensed directly
      under this License, not under broader terms of your package).

  This dependency permission includes direct and transitive dependencies, as
  well as Software bundled into or distributed with packages solely to enable
  a Permitted Use. In all cases, the Software remains subject to this License
  and may not be redistributed as a standalone product or Competitive Product.

  No other rights are granted, whether by implication, estoppel, or otherwise.
  In particular, except for the modification and dependency-distribution
  rights above, this License does not grant you rights to create derivative
  works for public or commercial distribution as a library, or to sublicense
  the Software except as necessary to deliver a Permitted Use (for example,
  bundling minified runtime code — including your Permitted Use modifications —
