III. RESTRICTIONS

  You may not, without prior written consent of the Copyright Holder:

  (a) use the Software for any purpose other than a Permitted Use;

  (b) use the Software to develop, operate, or distribute a Competitive Product;

  (c) fork, clone, or republish the Software’s source code as a separate
      public project, package, or repository, or otherwise distribute a fork
      or clone of the Software to third parties, except as expressly permitted
      under Section II;

  (d) modify the Software and distribute, publish, or sell the modified
      version (or a substantial portion of it) to third parties, except as
      expressly permitted under Section II for modifications included in a
      Permitted Use deployment;

  (e) reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble the Software in order to
      build a Competitive Product (interoperability analysis strictly limited
      to integrating the Software into a Permitted Use is not restricted by
      this clause where such restriction is prohibited by applicable law);

  (f) remove, obscure, or alter any proprietary notices, copyright notices,
      or branding included with the Software. This restriction does not require
      displaying the Copyright Holder’s branding or trademarks in the user
      interface of a Permitted Use deployment. Copyright and license notices
      must be retained in the Software distribution or accompanying
      documentation, where technically and reasonably practicable;

  (g) redistribute the Software on a standalone basis (including republishing
      it on package registries under another name or as a competing package),
      except as expressly allowed by Section II for dependency distribution
      or bundling inside a Permitted Use deployment.


